# examples/ui/08_overlay, played: the pause, pushed and blurred, and "Really
# quit?", drawn by the game scene itself -- each one's veil taking the clicks
# meant for what is under it, and its first button the focus. raylib's
# software renderer has no shaders, so the pause shows its veil and no blur
# here. See tests/e2e/script.h for the grammar.

# --- the pause: a scene of its own -----------------------------------------

# The balls bounce from the first frame. The HUD is in the top right corner.
20 shot playing

# Pause, with the mouse: down on 21, up on 22, and PauseScene is pushed at
# the end of 22.
21 click 730 42
22 expect scene PauseScene

# Under the veil nothing takes a click: not the HUD's Quit, not the veil
# itself. And the balls have stopped, because a pushed scene freezes what is
# under it.
24 click 730 98
26 click 100 400
32 expect scene PauseScene
32 shot paused

# Resume has the focus: Enter alone.
33 tap KEY_ENTER
33 expect scene GameScene

# --- the dialog: an overlay and a panel, in the game scene ------------------

# Quit asks first. Nothing is pushed, so nothing stops: twenty frames on, the
# balls have moved behind the question.
35 click 730 98
46 shot really_quit
66 expect scene GameScene
66 shot the_game_goes_on

# A click on the veil, outside the panel, answers nothing. Stay has the
# focus, so Enter is the answer that loses nothing.
67 click 100 400
69 tap KEY_ENTER
80 shot stayed

# Asked again, and down to Quit: Enter ends the game, on the last frame.
81 click 730 98
83 tap KEY_DOWN
85 tap KEY_ENTER
85 end
